# Force LF line endings for all text files, regardless of the
# contributor's OS or editor settings. Without this, editing a .sh
# file on Windows (even in something like VS Code with default
# settings) can silently introduce CRLF line endings, which break
# Bash's parser on Linux with a "syntax error near unexpected token"
# on the very first function definition — this happened to two
# scripts in this repo before this file was added.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
